    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d68">

                <pb facs="0185" n="113" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg113"/>

                <head>No. 68.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr.
                    Martinez</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-01-16"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 16,
                        1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In acknowledging the receipt of your
                    excellency’s note of the 10th instant, permit me to convey to you my
                    gratification in receiving your assurance that the Government of Chili, in its
                    attitude toward the Calderon Government in Peru and in its treatment of
                    President Calderon, had no intention or purpose to impair in any way the state
                    of friendship and cordiality which has always existed between it and the
                    Government of the United States, and which it is the sincere wish of this
                    government may be perpetual.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
